Percussion Spirit: I... I hear it. The depth. The gravity. You understand the secret of matter, little Guardian. You played with mass to tame the frequency.
	
Game: Concept validated: The Influence of Mass on Frequency
By adding water to the bronze bowls, you increased their overall mass. In acoustic physics, the more massive and heavy a resonating body is, the more it resists movement. It therefore vibrates more slowly, producing a low-frequency wave (a deep sound). Conversely, a light object vibrates quickly, creating a high-pitched sound.
	
